  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A disc is rolling without slipping on a surface. The radius of the disc is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>.</mo></math> At <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></math> the top most point on the disc is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> as shown in figure. When the disc completes half of its rotation, the displacement of point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> from its initial position is</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0021_ecdc729d64c6.png\" style=\"width: 380px; height: 210px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><msqrt><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><msqrt><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi><msqrt><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><img src=\"assets\\st0021_34ecef82d0b3.png\" style=\"width: 380px; height: 217px;\" /></p><p>The displacement is the hypotenuse of the diameter and the distance travelled for half the rotation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>R</mi></math>.</p><p>By using Pythagoras theorem,</p><p>Displacement of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>R</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><msqrt><msup><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></msqrt></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
